enticate as bbugyi200. Publication [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]requests name the commit their agent actually created, and existing[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]stale-revision rows are repaired explicitly. recovery-proof [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim](sase-1nf.10.1.9) closes with evidence, so the waiting [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]sase-1nf.10.1 land agent and then pub-recover (sase-1nf.11) resume [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]on a backlog that can drain.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]unblock_sase_1nf.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/unblock_sase_1nf.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1nv[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1nv/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Close gc-measure and hand its findings to gc-fix[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gc-closeout[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gc-closeout: finish sase-1nf.13 under the chosen scope, append the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]closure and handoff to the GC research report, leave a handoff note for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-1nf.14, and close only sase-1nf.13.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Apollo GitHub pushes authenticate as bbugyi200[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]ssh-identity[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ssh-identity: change the chezmoi-managed tailnet SSH config, get it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]applied on athena and apollo through a gate, verify the GitHub identity,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and close sase-1ni.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Publication requests name the committed revision[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]request-revision[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]request-revision: record the pre-dispatch HEAD separately, publish with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the post-commit SHA, give linked-repo rows page-only fulfillment in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-core, and add regression tests that fail on the old code.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Explicit repair for existing stale-revision outbox rows[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]stale-row-repair[dim] · [dim][/dim]after request-revision[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]stale-row-repair: add a report-first, audited `sase agent sync` repair [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that maps each stale requested revision to the agent's committed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]revision, or to linked scope, without dropping any request.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prove recovery on both hosts and close recovery-proof[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]pub-closeout[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ssh-identity, stale-row-repair[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pub-closeout: install the fixes on both hosts, run the repair, prove [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]checks 1 and 5 under the chosen canary policy, update the acceptance [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]report, then close sase-1nf.10.1.9.1 and sase-1nf.10.1.9.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1nv","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1nv.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-de145e3ea2601f7e3966122852500b5a","started_at":"202